<title>BRAZIL: Brazil soybean crop 80 pct harvested - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil soybean crop 80 pct harvested - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Around 80 percent of Brazil's expected soybean crop had been harvested by April 17, consultants Safras e Mercado said in a weekly report.</p>
<p>The 80 percent compares with 63 percent by April 18, 1996, and a historical average over the past five years of 57 percent, it added.</p>
<p>The harvest proceeded in an irregular fashion in the week ending April 17, mainly because of heavy rains in Mato Grosso, Mato Grosso do Sul and Bahia states.  </p>
<p>In other areas, rains did not get in the way of harvesting which was rapidly coming to an end and could be completed earlier than normal at the end of April.</p>
<p>The good news is that rains returned to Rio Grande do Sul state. But although rainfall was widespread, the losses caused by the recent dry spell were irreversible, Safras said.</p>
<p>A breakdown of percentage harvested by state follows.</p>
<p>									   5-yr</p>
<p> STATE		     17/04/97   10/04/97   18/04/96     avg</p>
<p> Rio Grande do Sul	 64	    57	   29	  34</p>
<p> Parana			94	    86	   89	  86</p>
<p> Mato Grosso		 90	    80	   76	  70</p>
<p> Mato Grosso do Sul	92	    80	   82	  74</p>
<p> Goias			 83	    72	   78	  50</p>
<p> Sao Paulo		  100	    98	   99	  91</p>
<p> Minas Gerais		55	    40	   42	  39</p>
<p> Others			50	    30	   28	  30</p>
<p> TOTAL BRAZIL		80	    70	   63	  57</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
